<newsitem itemid="169228" id="root" date="1996-11-06" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: FNB year profits hit by bad debt charge.</title>
<headline>FNB year profits hit by bad debt charge.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended Setember 30</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)	  228.0	 vs   210.4</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	    229.8	 vs   198.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			 76	   vs    66</p>
<p>    Attrib income		1,000.4	 vs   865.2</p>
<p>    Net interest income	3,575.1	 vs 2,976.7</p>
<p>    Other operating income   2,968.8	 vs 2,514.8</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge   665.2	 vs   393.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			1,506.7	 vs 1,436.9</p>
<p>    Tax				543.2	 vs   608.9</p>
<p>Div payable Dec 10</p>
<p>On register Nov 22</p>
<p>Full name: First National Bank Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast headline earnings rising to between 243 and 252 cents a share with a consensus of 247.8 cents. They expected a dividend of 77.4 cents.</p>
<p>The difference between headline and attributable earnings reflects profits on the sale of fixed assets plus goodwill.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
